<section class="section-tight">
  <div class="container article-body">
    <p>This Privacy Policy explains how VidhiCorp Legal Chambers ("we", "us", "the chambers") collects, uses and protects information when you visit this website or submit information through our enquiry, intake, careers or newsletter forms.</p>

    <h2>Information we collect</h2>
    <p>We collect information you voluntarily provide through our forms — such as your name, email address, phone number, company name and details of your enquiry or matter — and standard technical information collected automatically through analytics, such as pages visited, device and browser type, and approximate location, via Google Analytics.</p>

    <h2>How we use your information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To respond to enquiries, consultation requests and matter intake submissions.</li>
      <li>To process careers applications.</li>
      <li>To send Legal Updates and Legal Insights to newsletter subscribers, where you have opted in.</li>
      <li>To understand website usage and improve its content and performance.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not sell or rent personal information to third parties. Information submitted through our forms is processed via Formspree, our form-handling service provider, and is used solely to deliver your submission to the chambers.</p>

    <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
    <p>This website uses Google Analytics (GA4) to understand aggregate visitor behaviour. Google Analytics uses cookies and similar technologies; you can control or disable cookies through your browser settings. We do not use this data to individually identify visitors for marketing purposes.</p>

    <h2>Confidentiality</h2>
    <p>Any information shared with us in connection with a potential or existing matter is treated as confidential in accordance with our professional obligations as advocates, and is not disclosed to third parties except as required to advise on or represent you in that matter, or as required by law.</p>

    <h2>Data retention</h2>
    <p>We retain enquiry and matter-related information for as long as reasonably necessary to respond to your enquiry, provide services, or comply with our legal and professional obligations.</p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>You may request access to, correction of, or deletion of personal information you have submitted to us, by writing to us at the contact details below, subject to any professional or legal obligations that require us to retain certain records.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>For questions about this Privacy Policy, write to us at <a href="mailto:{{ site.primaryEmail }}">{{ site.primaryEmail }}</a>.</p>

    <p class="mt-32" style="font-size:13px;color:var(--text-muted);border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding-top:24px">This policy may be updated from time to time to reflect changes in our practices or applicable law.</p>
